# Windows batch scripts must keep CRLF line endings: cmd.exe mis-parses a
# multi-line block that has been converted to LF. Without this, a clone on
# macOS/Linux (or a repo configured with core.autocrlf=input) would check out
# working-looking .bat files that fail at the first `if (` block.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
